The second generation, introduced on 11 December 2019 at Mercedes media event,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://media.mercedes-benz.com/article/c148055e-b14b-4fdb-87bc-6565c47dda36 |title=Der neue Mercedes-Benz GLA feiert seine digitale Weltpremiere auf Mercedes me media |date=11 December 2019 |language=de |work=Daimler AG}}</ref> is revised from the previous generation. The chassis number, 247, is shared with [[Mercedes-Benz B-Class|W247 B-Class]] and [[Mercedes-Benz GLB|X247 GLB]]. The GLA uses the second generation MFA2 platform and completes the eight-model [[Mercedes-Benz A-Class (W177)|W177 A-Class]] compact based line-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://jalopnik.com/the-2021-mercedes-benz-gla-250-is-bigger-and-has-221-hp-1840361060 |last=Lee |first=Kristen |date=11 December 2019 |title=The 2021 Mercedes-Benz GLA 250 Is Bigger And Has 221 HP |work=Jalopnik}}</ref>

The H247 GLA is {{convert|15|mm|in|abbr=on}} shorter in length, {{convert|10|mm|in|abbr=on}} narrower, {{convert|104|mm|in|abbr=on}} higher than the first-generation model, and the wheelbase has been extended by {{convert|30|mm|in|abbr=on}}.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.wardsauto.com/technology/mercedes-benz-reveals-new-gla-crossover|title=Mercedes-Benz Reveals New GLA Crossover|date=2019-12-10|website=WardsAuto|language=en|access-date=2019-12-27}}</ref> The H247 GLA has 116&nbsp;mm more headroom, 45&nbsp;mm more elbow room and 43&nbsp;mm more rear shoulder room.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://citizen.co.za/motoring/motoring-news-motoring/2217953/new-mercedes-benz-gla-revealed-along-with-hot-amg-gla-35/|title=New Mercedes-Benz GLA revealed along with hot AMG GLA 35|website=citizen.co.za|date=11 December 2019 |access-date=2019-12-27}}</ref> The ground clearance has been raised by 9&nbsp;mm to 143&nbsp;mm and the front seats are positioned 140&nbsp;mm higher than in the W177 A-Class. Despite this, there is an added {{convert|22|mm|in|abbr=on}} of front-seat headroom compared to its predecessor.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/new-cars/new-mercedes-gla-receives-more-tech-space-and-comfort|title=New Mercedes GLA receives more tech, space and comfort {{!}} Autocar|website=www.autocar.co.uk|access-date=2019-12-27}}</ref>

As with other MFA2-based models, the GLA has suspension with [[MacPherson strut]]s up front and either a [[torsion beam]] or [[multi-link suspension]] at the rear. Variable damping control is optional.<ref name=":1" /> Inside, the GLA is similar to other MFA2 Mercedes models, featuring a dashboard with a free-standing digital display panel, the MBUX infotainment system, as well as other tech such as a colour Heads-Up Display.<ref name=":0" />

A [[Battery electric vehicle|battery electric]] version called the [[Mercedes-Benz EQA|EQA]] was introduced in 2020 as the third battery electric SUV from Mercedes-Benz.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.auto-motor-und-sport.de/neuheiten/mercedes-eqa-2020/ |title=Mercedes EQA 2020 |last=Wittich |first=Horst |date=12 December 2019 |language=de |work=auto motor und sport}}</ref><gallery widths="200" heights="130">
